WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.080
A liquid painted on teeth stops cavities in young children without drilling or anesthesia. This

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:11.340
is Planetarian Daily, episode 225. Women's heart care across a lifetime, the real cost

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:17.300
of two drinks a day, an aspirin that only helps one genotype. A major clinical trial tested

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:22.040
that liquid during routine visits, and found decay halted after it was applied in seconds.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:27.280
The treatment needs no injections. Science Daily reports the inexpensive painting could

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.600
spare thousands of children, painful dental procedures and surgery.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:36.560
The same trial is meant to support wider regulatory review and broader food and drug administration

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:37.520
approved use.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.640
The liquid fits into ordinary appointments rather than operating rooms.

00:00:42.677 --> 00:00:47.997
American Heart Association clinicians join the American Academy of Pediatrics, the Society

00:00:47.997 --> 00:00:52.817
for Maternal Fetal Medicine, and the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists

00:00:52.817 --> 00:00:55.637
on a single cardiovascular framework for women.

00:00:55.637 --> 00:01:00.457
The guidance divides women's heart care into four phases from childhood through older

00:01:00.457 --> 00:01:02.457
age, according to stat news.

00:01:03.017 --> 00:01:07.697
The societies wrote it to close gaps that remain even after female only trial requirements

00:01:07.697 --> 00:01:09.097
began in 1993.

00:01:09.957 --> 00:01:15.177
Differences in heart muscle chromosomes, symptom presentation, and disease causes between women

00:01:15.177 --> 00:01:18.237
and men are the stated reasons for one coordinated approach.

00:01:18.917 --> 00:01:21.897
Three supporting articles appeared in circulation the same day.

00:01:21.897 --> 00:01:27.217
The society's aim to unite clinicians and patients over a lifetime of care, with the

00:01:27.217 --> 00:01:31.837
explicit goal of reducing cardiovascular disease as the leading cause of death in women.

00:01:32.457 --> 00:01:37.657
Wide gaps in care across specialties persist even after those chromosome and symptom differences

00:01:37.657 --> 00:01:39.417
were already documented in trials.

00:01:40.372 --> 00:01:45.192
Most people assume two alcoholic drinks a day fall in a safe or even protective range.

00:01:45.712 --> 00:01:51.712
A large analysis instead ties that intake to a lifetime chance of one in 25 of dying

00:01:51.712 --> 00:01:53.272
from alcohol-related causes.

00:01:54.409 --> 00:01:58.869
Science Daily reports no significant overall health benefit across consumption levels.

00:01:59.669 --> 00:02:04.309
Risk grows steadily as intake increased, and the curve kept climbing beyond two drinks.

00:02:05.029 --> 00:02:09.469
The work challenged the idea that moderate drinking is harmless by isolating alcohol's

00:02:09.469 --> 00:02:11.009
own contribution to mortality.

00:02:11.769 --> 00:02:16.189
Researchers tracked outcomes across varying intake amounts rather than treating a moderate

00:02:16.189 --> 00:02:17.909
band as a special safe zone.

00:02:17.909 --> 00:02:18.009
1.

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:21.881
Alcohol acts through several roots inside the body at once.

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:24.081
It damages liver cells directly.

00:02:24.621 --> 00:02:26.561
It disrupts the regulation of heart rhythm.

00:02:27.101 --> 00:02:29.421
It raises blood pressure gradually over years.

00:02:30.021 --> 00:02:34.641
Those processes accumulate even when intake stays at moderate levels on most days of the

00:02:34.641 --> 00:02:34.841
week.

00:02:35.441 --> 00:02:40.381
The 1 in 25 figure comes from population-level tracking that compared death records against

00:02:40.381 --> 00:02:41.921
self-reported drinking patterns.

00:02:42.441 --> 00:02:47.561
The analysis separated alcohol attributable causes from other mortality, so the drink

00:02:47.561 --> 00:02:50.501
itself, not the rest of a lifestyle, carried the count.

00:02:51.341 --> 00:02:55.741
Evening routines and social habits that many treat as ordinary, sit at the intake level

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:56.621
the study measured.

00:02:57.201 --> 00:03:01.801
Follow-up that separates genetic susceptibility from average population effects would show

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:03.901
who faces the steepest part of that curve.

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:09.081
The absence of any net health benefit across the full range of consumption removes the older

00:03:09.081 --> 00:03:11.381
claim that small amounts confer protection.

00:03:12.376 --> 00:03:17.176
Older adults carrying a particular genetic profile showed a marked drop in dementia risk

00:03:17.176 --> 00:03:18.856
while taking low dose aspirin.

00:03:19.496 --> 00:03:23.616
The relative reduction in that defined subgroup reached 70%.

00:03:23.616 --> 00:03:28.216
Earlier studies found no overall protective effect when the same dose was examined across

00:03:28.216 --> 00:03:29.416
broader populations.

00:03:30.096 --> 00:03:33.456
No comparable effect emerged without genotype stratification.

00:03:34.156 --> 00:03:38.256
Genetics may therefore explain why benefits appear in some people and not in others.

00:03:38.836 --> 00:03:43.176
The reduction was measured inside a defined genetic subgroup within the larger cohort,

00:03:43.736 --> 00:03:45.116
not in the cohort as a whole.

00:03:45.116 --> 00:03:50.947
Pancreatic cancer cells continually reshape their genetic makeup in laboratory experiments,

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:53.447
becoming more aggressive and more resistant.

00:03:54.007 --> 00:03:58.667
The cells altered DNA structure repeatedly during growth and during exposure to treatment

00:03:59.027 --> 00:03:59.367
conditions.

00:03:59.887 --> 00:04:02.847
Blocking one key gene reversed several of those changes.

00:04:03.427 --> 00:04:08.127
That gene block was enough in the lab to undo multiple resistance-related modifications.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:12.267
The finding points to a potential route for new therapeutic strategies.

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:12.427
universities.

00:04:13.159 --> 00:04:17.859
University of Waterloo scientists created a gel that mimics the sea cucumber's ability

00:04:17.859 --> 00:04:19.859
to alter body stiffness on demand.

00:04:20.399 --> 00:04:25.139
Fizz.org reports the material is meant to support damaged tendons and other soft tissues

00:04:25.139 --> 00:04:25.839
during healing.

00:04:26.359 --> 00:04:26.959
Then degrade.

00:04:27.519 --> 00:04:29.479
It leaves no permanent implant behind.

00:04:30.099 --> 00:04:34.739
The gel changes stiffness in response to local conditions, modeled on the invertebrates

00:04:34.739 --> 00:04:36.259
documented tissue behavior.

00:04:36.799 --> 00:04:41.259
Development focused on matching mechanical support during the repair phase without residual

00:04:41.259 --> 00:04:41.839
material.

00:04:41.839 --> 00:04:47.478
Temporary support is intended exactly where tissue is damaged, then the gel breaks down

00:04:47.478 --> 00:04:48.698
once repair is complete.

00:04:49.218 --> 00:04:52.598
The design aims to cut complications tied to permanent implants.

00:04:53.278 --> 00:04:58.198
How the gel holds up under repeated mechanical stress in larger animal models remains an open

00:04:58.198 --> 00:05:00.238
question before human testing begins.

00:05:01.277 --> 00:05:05.777
Carry on crows identified the direction of moving dots and responded while keeping high

00:05:05.777 --> 00:05:06.357
accuracy.

00:05:07.017 --> 00:05:11.657
University of Tubingen researchers tested two of the birds on that moving dot task.

00:05:11.657 --> 00:05:15.977
The Crow's average 235 milliseconds to decide and act.

00:05:16.397 --> 00:05:21.337
That speed is roughly twice the speed recorded for humans and monkeys under comparable conditions.

00:05:21.917 --> 00:05:26.237
The experiment presented dot patterns moving in different directions and required each

00:05:26.237 --> 00:05:28.217
crow to indicate the direction it perceived.

00:05:28.877 --> 00:05:31.857
High accuracy held even at the faster decision speed.

00:05:32.872 --> 00:05:36.992
Yale researchers applied machine learning to fossil measurements from ancient reptiles

00:05:36.992 --> 00:05:40.172
and classified spinosaurus as predominantly aquatic.

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:42.832
The model ran on thousands of measurements.

00:05:43.572 --> 00:05:48.652
Science Daily reports that some species previously assumed to be fully aquatic still spent substantial

00:05:48.652 --> 00:05:49.572
time on land.

00:05:50.032 --> 00:05:54.712
The algorithm compared skeletal features across many specimens to infer habitat use.

00:05:55.412 --> 00:06:00.132
Results put Spinosaurus underwater for most of its life, while certain marine reptiles

00:06:00.132 --> 00:06:02.272
retain significant terrestrial activity.

00:06:03.228 --> 00:06:08.088
In brief, a family nurse practitioner in stat news describes patients with normal labs

00:06:08.088 --> 00:06:13.068
and vital signs, who report declining energy and stamina compared with earlier decades,

00:06:13.468 --> 00:06:17.548
and notes that normal aging and life demands are sometimes misread as illness.

00:06:18.128 --> 00:06:23.348
The Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine, as covered by drug discovery news, recognizes

00:06:23.348 --> 00:06:28.088
work that enabled precise control of neurons with light and advanced the mapping of brain

00:06:28.088 --> 00:06:28.568
circuits.

00:06:29.028 --> 00:06:33.948
Before we go, that CQ-Cumber Gel still has to be tested under repeated mechanical stress

00:06:33.948 --> 00:06:37.048
in larger animal models before human testing can begin.

